menu "AD Wearable Node Configuration"

    choice DEVICE_ROLE
        prompt "Device role"
        default DEVICE_ROLE_SKIN_PATCH
        help
            One firmware image, two build targets -- matches
            docs/hardware_architecture_v3_2026-09-18.md's two-node split. Run
            `idf.py menuconfig` and pick the role before flashing each physical device;
            this is a compile-time choice, not something the firmware detects at runtime.

        config DEVICE_ROLE_WRISTBAND
            bool "Wristband (BMI270 accel+gyro + PPG)"
            help
                Motion + pulse node. Feeds the deployed WESAD stress model's BVP-derived
                features and a future scratch-quantification model (Section "Wristband"
                of hardware_architecture_v3).

        config DEVICE_ROLE_SKIN_PATCH
            bool "Skin patch (moisture + temperature + EDA)"
            help
                Skin-surface sensing node. Feeds the planned moisture channel and the
                WESAD stress model's EDA/TEMP features (Section "Skin patch" of
                hardware_architecture_v3).

        config DEVICE_ROLE_IMAGING_GATE
            bool "Imaging capture gate (distance + ambient light + LED ring)"
            help
                Standardized-acquisition node for the robustness/hardware research
                question (docs/imaging_capture_gate_design_2026-09-19.md) -- not part of
                hardware_architecture_v3's original two-node plan. Reports READY over BLE
                once distance and illumination are both within tolerance; does not take
                the photo itself (built for a plain ESP32, no confirmed camera module).
    endchoice

    choice SENSOR_BACKEND
        prompt "Sensor backend"
        default SENSOR_BACKEND_SIMULATED
        help
            No physical sensors exist for this project yet (see the honors-project chat
            log this firmware was scaffolded from). SIMULATED lets every layer above the
            I2C/ADC driver -- windowing, BLE packaging, the phone-side client -- be built
            and tested honestly before any hardware exists. Switch to REAL once actual
            parts are wired up; nothing above sensor_hal.h needs to change to do that.

        config SENSOR_BACKEND_SIMULATED
            bool "Simulated (synthetic waveforms, no hardware required)"

        config SENSOR_BACKEND_REAL
            bool "Real sensors (BMI270 / MAX30101-class PPG / moisture / EDA front end)"
            help
                Not implemented yet -- sensor_hal_real.c is a stub that fails loudly at
                init time. Fill in the actual I2C/ADC driver calls once parts are on hand;
                see sensor_hal.h for the exact interface every backend must implement.
    endchoice

endmenu
